Subject: [PATCH 08610/11362] Phase 4: redirect 4a (stale premise), diagnose
 Mode A's real error class

4a's premise ("trust() gates the CNN prior out") checked before building and
found stale: gated_engine_from_transitions's cell-recall gate already passes
in production (sp80, heldout_cell_recall=0.98-1.0), and REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-14
through -20 already root-caused the real downstream bottleneck -- a trusted,
gate-passing dynamics model still yields no plan, traced to zero-gradient
goal-energy for never-completed levels, unfixed by 5x budget or a novelty-
energy fallback. Retraining an already-98%-accurate model for marginally
better accuracy is unlikely to move a bottleneck that persists at near-
perfect accuracy.

Redirected to the 2026-07-29 admission-bottleneck note's own named next
step: characterize Mode A's error class (REQ-ARC-WMTE-6244). Four distinct
root causes across ar25/ka59/re86/cd82, none of them prediction quality:

- ar25: sophisticated block-sliding logic, crashes on a scalar-into-list-
  slice TypeError (mechanical codegen bug, not a design flaw)
- ka59: hardcoded absolute-coordinate memorization from induce-time
  examples, zero generalization
- re86: plausible dynamics logic gated behind a wrong action-modality
  assumption (expects click+coords, real invocations are keyboard-style)
- cd82: keyboard actions completely unmodeled, click action writes a
  context-free fixed color

Bonus adversarial check: cd82 superficially passes the shipped nav
template's confidence gate but scores 0 held-out exact-match, reproduced
across two independent samples -- a genuine false-positive gap in
is_confident_nav, not a hidden win.

Analysis only, CPU-only, no code shipped. determination_preservation_lint,
adversarial_verify, artifact_freshness_lint all clean.
